<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Đurađ Branković</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1377–1456</span> · Also known as George Branković</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Đurađ Branković was Despot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> from 1427 to 1456. He built the great fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smederevo">Smederevo</a> as his capital on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>, balancing between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. The Ottomans overran Serbia in 1439, but he recovered it in 1444. Serbia fell to the Ottomans three years after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/durad-brankovic.jpg" alt="Đurađ Branković" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C4%90ura%C4%91_Brankovi%C4%87,_Esphigmenou_charter_(1429).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
